id: pm-gh1555
title: "GH-1555: refuse assignment-only linked-test commands before recording false passes"
description: "The October23 report shows test --add status=passed being interpreted as a shell assignment, then recorded as passing without executing a test. Investigate strict linked-command admission and typed metadata-typo recovery without restricting legitimate environment-prefixed executable commands."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: context-management,"gh:1555",sdk
created_at: "2026-10-23T07:34:02.529Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T11:30:09.447Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-23T11:30:08.643Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-23T11:30:08.643Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: A current SDK/CLI regression reproduces assignment-only false pass admission; Refusal or no-executable verdict is typed and actionable before false success is recorded; Environment-prefixed real commands and sandbox/trust controls remain supported.
parent: pm-gh1469
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: Shared SDK admission rejects plain assignment-only commands at registration and legacy execution; selected effective entries are checked under the write lock before combined edits persist.
expected_result: Refuse metadata-only commands without durable writes or false pass receipts while retaining executable environment prefixes and explicit selectors.
actual_result: Linked suite passes 42 tests; focused regressions and installed npm/npx plus bun/bunx consumers verify refusal without writes and valid execution. Static components pass; GitHub full coverage and required checks remain merge conditions.
